# Intel xRX500 packet datapath.
#
# INTEL_XRX500_NET is separate from LANTIQ_XRX200 because INTEL_MIPS and
# LANTIQ are mutually exclusive entries in arch/mips/Kconfig's "System
# type" choice, so this port cannot depend on SOC_TYPE_XWAY.

menuconfig INTEL_XRX500_NET
	bool "Intel xRX500 / GRX350 ethernet drivers"
	depends on INTEL_MIPS && OF && HAS_IOMEM
	default n
	help
	  Selects the packet datapath of the Intel xRX500 family: the buffer
	  manager that owns the segment pools and the egress queues, the DMA
	  controllers that move frames between them and the switch macros, and
	  the network device that carries the processor's end of it.

	  The switch macros themselves are driven as DSA switches and are
	  configured under Distributed Switch Architecture instead.

	  Say N here unless you are building for a GRX350-class board such as
	  the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560.

if INTEL_XRX500_NET

config INTEL_XRX500_BM
	bool "xRX500 packet buffer manager"
	default n
	help
	  The central buffer manager, the traffic manager it dequeues
	  through, and the packet DMA controllers. Together they own the
	  reserved segment pools every frame is carried in, the free-segment
	  queue those segments are drawn from and returned to, and the
	  per-port egress resources a frame is enqueued on.

	  Not a module: the buffer economy is a set of reserved memory
	  regions the driver maintains by hand, and the MIPS cache
	  maintenance that takes is not exported to modules.

	  Say N unless you are bringing this datapath up.

config INTEL_XRX500_CBM_CONDUIT
	bool "xRX500 buffer-manager conduit network device"
	depends on INTEL_XRX500_BM
	default n
	help
	  Conduit network device for the xRX500 central buffer manager: one
	  netdev per switch macro whose transmit path enqueues into the
	  buffer manager and whose receive path terminates that macro's own
	  receive DMA ring.

	  This is what a DSA switch driver for the macros binds as its
	  conduit; without it the switch has no processor port.

	  Say N unless you are bringing this datapath up.

endif # INTEL_XRX500_NET
